.TH KROT 1 "" "krot" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
krot \- manage WireGuard and AmneziaWG tunnels on Linux servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krot
.I action
.RI [ flags ]
.PP
Exactly one action is required per invocation. Flags use the long forms
.B \-\-flag value
or
.BR \-\-flag = value .
Run
.B krot \-\-help
for a compact command summary.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B krot
creates, deletes, starts, and stops WireGuard and AmneziaWG 1.x, 2.0, and 3.1
tunnels. It manages clients without restarting or recreating the interface and
prints client configurations, QR codes, AmneziaVPN keys, and KeeneticOS commands.
.PP
The interface configuration is the single source of truth. Client operations use
only targeted
.B wg
or
.B awg set
peer calls, so other connected clients are unaffected.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list
List tunnels. Supports filters and table or JSON output.
.TP
.B \-\-create
Create a tunnel, write its configuration atomically, and enable its systemd unit.
.TP
.B \-\-delete
Delete a tunnel after confirmation when it has clients. Use
.B \-\-yes
to skip the question.
.TP
.BR \-\-up , " " \-\-down
Start or stop an existing interface through its systemd unit.
.TP
.B \-\-add\-client
Create a client and print its configuration. Optional output includes a QR code,
an AmneziaVPN key, and KeeneticOS CLI commands.
.TP
.B \-\-delete\-client
Delete a client from the configuration and a running interface.
.TP
.BR \-\-lock\-client , " " \-\-unlock\-client
Disable or restore a client without changing other peers.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-client
List clients, addresses, status, latest handshake, and traffic counters.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Read-only environment diagnostics. This action does not require root and does
not take the global lock.
.TP
.B \-\-udp\-listener
Run a UDP diagnostic listener on one port or a range of ports.
.TP
.B \-\-udp\-checker
Check a remote krot UDP listener and report packet loss and round-trip time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command help. Does not require root.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, commit, and build date. Does not require root.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " wg|awg|awg2|awg3"
Protocol type. Required for creation; optional as a list filter.
.TP
.BI \-\-interface " NAME"
Interface name, up to 15 characters matching
.BR [a-zA-Z0-9_.=+-] .
Required by most tunnel and client actions; optional as a list filter.
.TP
.BI \-\-ip " CIDR[,CIDR]"
Server addresses for creation, client addresses for addition, or an address
filter for listing. One IPv4 and one IPv6 address are allowed. Client addresses
use /32 and /128 prefixes.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N|N:M"
UDP port or inclusive port range from 1 to 65535. UDP diagnostics accept at most
1024 ports. Required for creation and UDP modes; optional as a list filter.
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " HOST"
Public server address for client configurations, without a port. Required for
creation and a per-client override during addition.
.TP
.BI \-\-address " HOST"
Remote listener address for the UDP checker, without a port.
.TP
.BI \-\-mtu " N"
MTU from 576 to 9000. Defaults: wg 1420, awg/awg2 1376, awg3 1280.
.TP
.BI \-\-dns " IP[,IP]"
DNS servers for generated client configurations.
.TP
.BI \-\-i1 " CPS"
AmneziaWG I1 signature packet, at most 2048 characters. Valid only for awg types
and incompatible with
.BR \-\-mimic .
.TP
.BI \-\-mimic " PROFILE"
Generate an I1-I5 mimicry chain. Profiles are
.BR dns , " " stun , " " ntp , " " ssdp , " and " dtls .
Valid only for awg types.
.TP
.BI \-\-id " ID"
Client identifier, 1 to 64 characters matching
.BR [a-zA-Z0-9_.-] ,
unique within an interface.
.TP
.BI \-\-allowed\-ips " CIDR[,CIDR]"
AllowedIPs value written to the client configuration, for example
.BR 0.0.0.0/0,::/0 .
.TP
.B \-\-psk
Generate a PresharedKey for the client.
.TP
.B \-\-qr
Also print the client configuration as a terminal QR code.
.TP
.B \-\-amnezia\-key
Also print the client configuration as an AmneziaVPN
.B vpn://
key.
.TP
.B \-\-keenetic
Also print KeeneticOS CLI commands. Supports wg and awg 1.0/1.5/2.0 with IPv4
only; awg3 is not supported.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print JSON instead of a table for list, list-client, and UDP modes. JSON keys,
status values, and detail values are not localized.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation when deleting a tunnel.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Response timeout for one UDP packet, for example
.B 2s
or
.BR 500ms .
The default is 2s.
.TP
.BI \-\-count " N"
Packets of each type per UDP port, from 1 to 100. The default is 3.
.TP
.BI \-\-echo\-size " N"
Random echo payload size from 1 to 1400 bytes. The default is 64.
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Concurrent UDP port checks from 1 to 100. The default is 32. Requests within one
port remain sequential.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Write UDP diagnostic progress to standard error without changing standard output.
.SH UDP DIAGNOSTICS
The listener accepts
.B ping SEQ:N
and returns
.BR "pong SEQ:N" ;
it returns the payload of
.B ECHO text
and replies to
.B TIME
with Unix time in milliseconds. The protocol is unencrypted.
.PP
The checker reports
.B ok
when all ping and echo replies are valid,
.B filtered
when a reply times out, and
.B error
for an invalid response or local network error. SIGINT or SIGTERM prints results
for completed ports only and exits with status 10.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LC_ALL
Highest-priority locale selection variable.
.TP
.B LC_MESSAGES
Used when LC_ALL is empty or unset.
.TP
.B LANG
Used when both variables above are empty or unset.
.PP
The supported languages are English (en_US) and Russian (ru_RU). A locale whose
name is ru or begins with ru followed by _, -, ., or @ selects Russian. All other
values, including C and POSIX, select English. Command names, flags, JSON,
configuration files, KeeneticOS commands, shell completion, and the UDP protocol
are not localized. Errors from the operating system and external programs are
preserved verbatim.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Internal or unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Invalid value.
.TP
.B 4
Interface or client not found.
.TP
.B 5
Conflict: an object already exists, or an address or port is in use.
.TP
.B 6
Environment error: missing privileges, tools, or a required AmneziaWG version.
.TP
.B 7
Could not acquire the global lock.
.TP
.B 10
Canceled by the user.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/wireguard/*.conf
WireGuard interface configurations.
.TP
.I /etc/amnezia/amneziawg/*.conf
AmneziaWG interface configurations.
.TP
.I /run/lock/krot.lock
Global krot lock.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/krot.1
English manual page.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/ru/man1/krot.1
Russian manual page.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create an AmneziaWG 2.0 tunnel:
.PP
.nf
sudo krot \-\-create \-\-type awg2 \-\-ip 10.8.0.1/24 \e
    \-\-port 51820 \-\-endpoint vpn.example.com
.fi
.PP
Add a client and display a QR code:
.PP
.nf
sudo krot \-\-add\-client \-\-interface awg0 \-\-id phone \e
    \-\-allowed\-ips 0.0.0.0/0,::/0 \-\-qr
.fi
.PP
Check a UDP port range with 64 workers and progress messages:
.PP
.nf
krot \-\-udp\-checker \-\-address 203.0.113.1 \e
    \-\-port 51820:51830 \-\-workers 64 \-\-verbose
.fi
.SH NOTES
Root is not required for help, version, doctor, or UDP checking. The UDP listener
requires root only for ports below 1024 or when /proc/net/udp and /proc/net/udp6
are unreadable. Other actions require root.
.PP
krot does not install WireGuard or AmneziaWG and does not configure NAT,
forwarding, firewall rules, or sysctl settings.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR wg (8),
.BR wg\-quick (8),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ip (8)
